WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
The face looks almost ordinary. Yet something is already wrong.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.000
The eyes and mouth have been turned within the face.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Now the altered features are suddenly hard to ignore.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.000
The parts never moved. Their orientation within the whole changed.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:33.000
This effect was first published in 1980. Similar patterns are not unique to faces.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:40.000
The unsettling part isn't the image. It's how confidently we interpret it. Follow the evidence.
